{"card_hash": "ad390177be1d7a0f05fed3b5ebda71a14835653d44615ebddf48bfe942e766b2", "channel": "0xMarioNawfal", "chars": 57726, "chars_all_clips": 57726, "chars_chosen_clips": 1200, "clip_count": 42, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/RoundtableSpace/status/2093658671515680919#t=238", "end": 358.136, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "9456aba55f4d6646865529dbf73fdec53837b3caf778768e81ebf1621adcca0b", "start": 238.501, "text": "So you can imagine that there has been an exponential growth in just the model size for large language models The large stands for that they're growing in size and that has been one of the key areas in which the models have been getting bet", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/RoundtableSpace/status/2093658671515680919#t=1151", "end": 1270.693, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "d4c542aa82ba0c826f9936a465508ff0038ef7a78f20ccea38af03327f483e57", "start": 1151.877, "text": "ways that we can make the model better So let's think let's talk about it a little bit Like this is a work we did in my lab last year Last summer, it was called Large Language Monkeys And it's kind of inspired by the Infinite Monkey Theorem", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/RoundtableSpace/status/2093658671515680919#t=2113", "end": 2232.201, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "edda39cff1377ac24256896ffae59ecd3d252a5fed80830e9fccfed54240e4b8", "start": 2113.474, "text": "I, I think the question is that is it because of the reasoning process or is it because of the things step by step the chain of thought? Is it like is it the data that's making the inference or is it the instruction? it's, I mean so the dat", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/RoundtableSpace/status/2093658671515680919#t=2572", "end": 2691.25, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "db2a9a9466984924b5c35bde9b0d32f09decd730bb38a43b00b7962a7ec3b438", "start": 2572.233, "text": "So like in several cases in simpler cases, you can achieve these end-to-end goals like deep research can be accomplished end-to-end But in most scenarios you're still having very static workflows So today, what exists is closer to agentic w", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/RoundtableSpace/status/2093658671515680919#t=3177", "end": 3296.666, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "5186abf6836d1a5552cfb1c4d6aa2493b887b909b4316dd7e542eb4e43082e52", "start": 3177.113, "text": "Oftentimes the users will not specify the problem well enough So asking clarifying the user intent so that it knows what to go look for and how to verify starts to become important. And in models like O3 I think they have seen a lot of thes", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "AI and ML", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/RoundtableSpace/status/2093658671515680919#t=238", "end": 358.136, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "9456aba55f4d6646865529dbf73fdec53837b3caf778768e81ebf1621adcca0b", "start": 238.501, "text": "So you can imagine that there has been an exponential growth in just the model size for large language models The large stands for that they're growing in size and that has been one of the key areas in which the models have been getting bet", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/RoundtableSpace/status/2093658671515680919#t=1151", "end": 1270.693, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "d4c542aa82ba0c826f9936a465508ff0038ef7a78f20ccea38af03327f483e57", "start": 1151.877, "text": "ways that we can make the model better So let's think let's talk about it a little bit Like this is a work we did in my lab last year Last summer, it was called Large Language Monkeys And it's kind of inspired by the Infinite Monkey Theorem", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/Roundt